Z||000003||stimpy||02-09-2001||03:36 PM||||Far out! I actually went to High School in Waterloo! That town is great! Of course I was there in mid eighties, but it shouldn't have turned into a slum, hehe. Waterloo is a huge center for expatriates, so the vast majority of folks speak english, and a lot of American-style goodies are available. (Home of the first drive-in McDonalds in Europe, and they have beer on the menu!)<BR>My advice is avoid driving at all costs, Belgian drivers are some of the worst and gas is unreal $. Public transportation is excellent and affordable. Plus hitch-hiking back in the day was a breeze.<P>Other then that, enjoy les moules provencals and the pommes-frites, and have a Stella Artois for me!<P>BTW, what are you doing for your summer job,and are they still hiring?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||william_thorniii||02-09-2001||05:53 PM||||Hank,<P>Please take time to sample all of the fine Belgian beers.  Hands down, the finest in the world.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||7
Z||000005||Hank is Here||02-09-2001||07:45 PM||||Thanks for the replies.  I am gonig to be working for Bristol Meyers Squibb, heck the office park that the place is in is pratically all American companies.  I will probably be the ugly American becuase I don't speak a word of French, I am trying to learn though. <BR>The whole goal for me this summer is to return to the States without a dime in my pocket.  I want to spend all the $$ on travel and some of those "fine Belgian beers" as WTIII put it.  <BR>Cliff maybe when I am over there I can pay you a visit to see the person who started this all.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||stimpy||02-10-2001||12:22 AM||||Don't sweat the "ugly American" thing. Since Brussels is the seat of NATO, SHAPE, and the EEC, it is a pretty cosmopolitan place. Make sure you check out the sound and light show in Grand Place, and have one of those beers at the Roi d'Espagne. You are gonna have a blast! Just be respectful of the folks, make sure you tip the bathroom attendants and the program girls at the movie theatres.||||reg||1
